WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:01.113
- We're back,

00:00:01.980 --> 00:00:06.220
with my nearest and dearest,
Cameron Diaz and Lucy Liu.

00:00:06.220 --> 00:00:11.220
So we grew, and we grew
up, and now we are moms.

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:14.950
Do you think you're a
different person now, Lucy,

00:00:14.950 --> 00:00:16.020
than you were then?

00:00:16.020 --> 00:00:18.450
Like, aside from us knowing
each other and our friendship,

00:00:18.450 --> 00:00:20.670
just you as a human?

00:00:20.670 --> 00:00:24.390
- I think in my twenties,
I felt very bulletproof

00:00:24.390 --> 00:00:27.490
and very, you know,

00:00:27.490 --> 00:00:28.940
I don't wanna say it was risk-taking

00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:29.840
'cause it was beyond that.

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:32.300
It was like, I didn't really
care if I lived or died,

00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:35.780
you know, I just didn't and I
lost my father a few years ago

00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:39.630
and I didn't really recognize the levels

00:00:39.630 --> 00:00:41.360
that we have in our lives.

00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:46.100
And you know, like he was a place in my,

00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:49.270
in my life that was always sort of a,

00:00:49.270 --> 00:00:51.500
kind of a roof, you know?

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:55.160
And so suddenly you feel like
the roof has been torn off

00:00:55.160 --> 00:00:56.387
and then you sort of recognize,

00:00:56.387 --> 00:00:59.230
"Oh, you know, I am now the roof."

00:00:59.230 --> 00:01:00.830
You know, and I happen to have a child,

00:01:00.830 --> 00:01:03.400
so I guess I'm the roof to that child.

00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:04.780
So now I really have to understand

00:01:04.780 --> 00:01:07.260
that I have to shelter
him and I have to show,

00:01:07.260 --> 00:01:09.420
I have a responsibility and it's,

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:10.770
it's a very powerful thing,

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:12.480
it's also terrifying.

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:15.320
If I think about it, I think
my heart was smaller back then,

00:01:15.320 --> 00:01:18.790
'cause it was sort of more
inclined to what I wanted to do,

00:01:18.790 --> 00:01:20.970
but now it's sort of like,
what do we want to do?

00:01:20.970 --> 00:01:23.420
And it feels, it feels good because I feel

00:01:23.420 --> 00:01:25.120
like a fuller person.

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:28.210
Like life seems a much more, you know,

00:01:28.210 --> 00:01:31.050
kind of colorful and wild

00:01:31.050 --> 00:01:34.290
because there's so many more
opportunities, as a mom,

00:01:34.290 --> 00:01:37.380
to kind of like discover and, you know,

00:01:37.380 --> 00:01:39.780
there's so much more curiosity with kids.

00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:41.440
And it's sort of, it's mind blowing,

00:01:41.440 --> 00:01:43.870
and it's actually more
terrifying in a way, you know,

00:01:43.870 --> 00:01:46.040
because you're also responsible
for this little person.

00:01:46.040 --> 00:01:46.873
- Highest stakes.

00:01:46.873 --> 00:01:48.060
- So it's like, oh my God,

00:01:48.060 --> 00:01:51.760
I thought I was on a ride
back then, a wild ride,

00:01:51.760 --> 00:01:54.730
but actually it's now that
it's even more intense.

00:01:54.730 --> 00:01:56.270
- Well you nailed it,
because you're just dealing

00:01:56.270 --> 00:01:59.050
with your own mortality
and all of the sudden

00:01:59.050 --> 00:02:02.510
when you have a kid, I don't
care if it sounds codependent,

00:02:02.510 --> 00:02:05.600
my kids are more meaningful
to me than my own life.

00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:08.480
- I think there's
something that, in our DNA,

00:02:08.480 --> 00:02:10.630
that gets triggered, you know,

00:02:10.630 --> 00:02:15.630
like that just clicks on
when you become a parent.

00:02:15.870 --> 00:02:19.400
You have to make sure that they survive.

00:02:19.400 --> 00:02:20.760
They have to, they go on.

00:02:20.760 --> 00:02:23.180
You, we will die.

00:02:23.180 --> 00:02:24.570
I'm sorry to get like morbid,

00:02:24.570 --> 00:02:27.049
and this is those times when Drew goes,

00:02:27.049 --> 00:02:30.520
(sighs) "Really you're gonna die?

00:02:30.520 --> 00:02:32.121
Do we have to talk about that?"

00:02:32.121 --> 00:02:32.954
(laughs) But, like.

00:02:32.954 --> 00:02:34.310
- For your first show
it's all about mortality.

00:02:34.310 --> 00:02:35.143
- I know.
(Cameron and Lucy laughing)

00:02:35.143 --> 00:02:36.307
I think I'm ready to talk about death.

00:02:36.307 --> 00:02:37.600
- CBS is like, "Wait a minute."

00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:40.960
- I think I'm no longer a young idiot

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:42.730
who thinks I am immortal,

00:02:42.730 --> 00:02:45.230
which I'm glad to know I'm
not, I wasn't the only one.

00:02:45.230 --> 00:02:47.890
I mean, I hurled myself around,

00:02:47.890 --> 00:02:51.050
I abused this carcass to no end.

00:02:51.050 --> 00:02:53.800
And I just thought, true,
I was gonna die young,

00:02:53.800 --> 00:02:54.680
so who cares?

00:02:54.680 --> 00:02:56.650
Live now and go for it.

00:02:56.650 --> 00:02:59.760
And now, yeah, I mean,
2020 will make you think

00:02:59.760 --> 00:03:00.710
about your mortality,

00:03:00.710 --> 00:03:02.950
children will make you
think about your mortality.

00:03:02.950 --> 00:03:04.767
- You know, my twenties,
it was just sort of like,

00:03:04.767 --> 00:03:06.920
"Here we go, yeah, all right.

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:08.270
Yep, jump on that?

00:03:08.270 --> 00:03:09.103
Gotcha.

00:03:09.103 --> 00:03:10.650
Oh, is that a wild horse?

00:03:10.650 --> 00:03:13.800
Oh cool. Yeah, no, I know
how to hold on for my life.

00:03:13.800 --> 00:03:14.830
Let's go." (laughs)

00:03:14.830 --> 00:03:16.800
You know?
- There's such a liberation

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:18.487
in that too though, you know?

00:03:18.487 --> 00:03:20.530
- Yeah, I'm so glad I did it all.

00:03:20.530 --> 00:03:24.050
- When I thought about
trying to accomplish

00:03:24.050 --> 00:03:26.940
something big in my life at another point,

00:03:26.940 --> 00:03:29.550
you two were the people I did it with.

00:03:29.550 --> 00:03:32.640
And so of course, what a natural fit

00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:35.610
that you're the two people
that came into my head

00:03:35.610 --> 00:03:37.290
and my heart when I thought,

00:03:37.290 --> 00:03:42.160
how would I like to honor this endeavor?

00:03:42.160 --> 00:03:44.283
I see myself with you guys.

00:03:46.790 --> 00:03:48.540
- Exactly what the world needs.

00:03:48.540 --> 00:03:51.710
They need your light, they
need your joyous-ness,

00:03:51.710 --> 00:03:54.090
they need your perspective.

00:03:54.090 --> 00:03:56.220
One of the things that I have always

00:03:56.220 --> 00:03:59.390
been in total awe of in you

00:03:59.390 --> 00:04:02.940
is your ability to take
in all the information,

00:04:02.940 --> 00:04:06.490
how quick you are to not just,
like, what's in front of you,

00:04:06.490 --> 00:04:11.490
but the nuances and the sort
of the humanity and intellect.

00:04:11.770 --> 00:04:14.790
You can, you read more books
than any person I know,

00:04:14.790 --> 00:04:19.790
you listen to more music,
you look at more art.

00:04:20.230 --> 00:04:24.190
You bring, you watch
more television and film.

00:04:24.190 --> 00:04:27.180
You're actually taking
in all the information

00:04:27.180 --> 00:04:28.980
and you're synthesizing it.

00:04:28.980 --> 00:04:32.530
And you're bringing it into
this really unique perspective

00:04:32.530 --> 00:04:36.680
that is all about how it
connects all of us together,

00:04:36.680 --> 00:04:38.670
even if it doesn't feel
like it has anything

00:04:38.670 --> 00:04:40.520
to do with one another

00:04:40.520 --> 00:04:44.940
and you bring it to the world
in this joyous, beautiful,

00:04:44.940 --> 00:04:48.180
like buoyant light, that is you.

00:04:48.180 --> 00:04:50.130
And you, it's a gift.

00:04:50.130 --> 00:04:52.420
It's like truly a gift
that you give the world.

00:04:52.420 --> 00:04:54.330
And you're gonna make the world a happier,

00:04:54.330 --> 00:04:56.830
better place by giving us that gift.

00:04:56.830 --> 00:04:59.440
- You have a big soul and a big heart

00:04:59.440 --> 00:05:01.920
and doing this show is
really special and wonderful

00:05:01.920 --> 00:05:03.640
because you have something to share

00:05:03.640 --> 00:05:06.370
and you have gone through
tough times in your life.

00:05:06.370 --> 00:05:07.830
You've had issues with your family,

00:05:07.830 --> 00:05:11.640
you've had issues with, you
know, like marriages, divorces.

00:05:11.640 --> 00:05:13.080
You have something to share.

00:05:13.080 --> 00:05:15.830
And I don't know that I can
say that about a lot of things.

00:05:15.830 --> 00:05:17.530
I've never been married,
I've never been divorced.

00:05:17.530 --> 00:05:19.200
I haven't done a lot of
the things that you have.

00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:21.117
So, to me, the experience that you have

00:05:21.117 --> 00:05:23.540
and that you have to share is exciting.

00:05:23.540 --> 00:05:26.210
And I think that you
should feel free to do that

00:05:26.210 --> 00:05:27.210
because that's who you are.

00:05:27.210 --> 00:05:29.720
You're a very open, generous person.

00:05:29.720 --> 00:05:32.543
- I asked you guys here so
I could honor you today.

00:05:32.543 --> 00:05:33.500
(Lucy laughs)

00:05:33.500 --> 00:05:34.857
That's what this was about for me.

00:05:34.857 --> 00:05:36.560
- Well.
- Yeah, but you can't honor us

00:05:36.560 --> 00:05:37.820
without us honoring you.

00:05:37.820 --> 00:05:40.080
This is the symbiotic relationship

00:05:40.080 --> 00:05:41.870
and you have to be able to give and take

00:05:41.870 --> 00:05:43.560
and understand that, a lot of times

00:05:43.560 --> 00:05:46.910
when I give a friend a
compliment, they can't take it.

00:05:46.910 --> 00:05:47.743
You know?

00:05:47.743 --> 00:05:50.080
And like, it's time for us to receive.

00:05:50.080 --> 00:05:53.296
- Well, as you said at one of my weddings,

00:05:53.296 --> 00:05:54.520
(Lucy and Cameron laughing)

00:05:54.520 --> 00:05:56.737
when you read the E. E. Cummings poem,

00:05:56.737 --> 00:05:59.780
"I Carry Your Heart in my Heart,"

00:05:59.780 --> 00:06:01.870
and I carry both of you in my heart.

00:06:01.870 --> 00:06:04.080
I always have, I always will.

00:06:04.080 --> 00:06:05.023
Thank you.

00:06:05.883 --> 00:06:07.780
- [Cameron] Thank you, no thank you.

00:06:07.780 --> 00:06:10.347
(all laughing)

00:06:10.347 --> 00:06:11.939
- And thank you.

00:06:11.939 --> 00:06:13.787
And thank you.
- And thank you.

00:06:13.787 --> 00:06:15.120
- And thank you.

00:06:18.930 --> 00:06:20.540
Listen, man.

00:06:20.540 --> 00:06:24.470
I'm gonna be thinking tonight in my bed,

00:06:24.470 --> 00:06:28.950
wondering how I got so lucky

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:32.543
to, like, live a life with you guys.

00:06:34.100 --> 00:06:36.243
Thank you more than words can ever say.

00:06:37.210 --> 00:06:39.360
- Can't wait to see
the rest of the season.

00:06:39.360 --> 00:06:42.610
(audience applauding)

00:06:49.700 --> 00:06:52.430
- We're gonna celebrate a lot
of things here on this show,

00:06:52.430 --> 00:06:54.672
and friendship is certainly one of them.

00:06:54.672 --> 00:06:57.339
(upbeat music)

